---
import AxesFigure from "./primitives/axes-figure.astro";
---

<AxesFigure
  captionSlot
  size="lg"
  title="Convex Isoquant"
  yLabel="Capital (K)"
  xLabel="Labour (L)"
>
  <path
    class="curve tone-s5"
    d="
      M 145 85
      C 165 120, 185 155, 225 190
      C 270 230, 330 265, 405 295
      C 455 315, 505 330, 545 340
    "
  ></path>

  <line class="tangent" x1="155" y1="100" x2="275" y2="235"></line>
  <line class="tangent" x1="335" y1="265" x2="475" y2="325"></line>

  <circle class="pt tone-ink" cx="205" cy="175" r="5"></circle>
  <circle class="pt tone-ink" cx="405" cy="295" r="5"></circle>

  <text class="point-label" x="185" y="165">
    A
  </text>
  <text class="point-label" x="415" y="290">
    B
  </text>

  <text class="curve-label tone-s5" x="350" y="225">
    Q₁
  </text>

  <text class="mrt-label" x="125" y="125">
    Steeper
  </text>
  <text class="mrt-label" x="450" y="310">
    Flatter
  </text>

  <Fragment slot="caption">
    A convex isoquant reflects diminishing MRTS: as more labour replaces
    capital, the amount of capital that can be given up for an additional unit
    of labour decreases.
  </Fragment>
</AxesFigure>

<style>
  .tangent {
    stroke: var(--text-muted);
    stroke-width: 1.4;
    stroke-dasharray: 5 5;
  }

  .point-label {
    fill: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .mrt-label {
    fill: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
</style>
